## KEYWORDS('Statistics','Sampling')

# First comes some stuff that appears at the beginning of every problem

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',  'PGML.pl',
    'parserPopUp.pl', 'PGchoicemacros.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

@event1 = (
    qq/A public opinion poll in Ohio wants to determine 
    whether registered voters in the state approve of a
    measure to ban smoking in all public areas.  They
    randomly select 50 voters in the state and ask whether
    they approve or disapprove of the measure./,
    qq/A public opinion poll in Ohio wants to determine
    whether registered voters in the state approve of a
    measure to ban smoking in all public areas.  They randomly
    select 50 voters from each county in the state and ask
    whether they approve or disapprove of the measure./
);
$pick1 = random(0, 1);

$dd1 = DropDown([ 'Simple Random Sample', 'Stratified Random Sample' ], $pick1);

@event2 = (
    qq/At a party there are 30 students over age 21 and 20
    students under age 21.  You randomly select 5 students to
    interview about attitudes toward alcohol./,
    qq/At a party there are 30 students over age 21 and 20
    students under age 21.  You randomly select 3 of those over
    21 and 2 of those under 21 to interview about attitudes
    toward alcohol./
);

$pick2 = random(0, 1);
$dd2 = DropDown([ 'Simple Random Sample', 'Stratified Random Sample' ], $pick2);

@event3 = (
    qq/The Ministry of Health in the Canadian Province of
    Ontario conducted the Ontario Health Survey by conducting interviews with 65,000 randomly selected residents of Ontario./,
    qq/The Ministry of Health in the Canadian Province of
    Ontario conducted the Ontario Health Survey by conducting
    interviews with 30,000 randomly selected men and 35,000
    randomly selected women who reside in Ontario./,
);
$pick3 = random(0, 1);
$dd3 = DropDown([ 'Simple Random Sample', 'Stratified Random Sample' ], $pick3);

BEGIN_PGML

For each of following scenarios determine if it is a simple random sample or stratified random sample. 

   
1) [$event1[$pick1]]

    This is an example of a [_]{$dd1}

2) [$event2[$pick2]]

    This is an example of a [_]{$dd2}

3) [$event3[$pick3]]

    This is an example of a [_]{$dd3}


END_PGML

